        "original_id": "46ac3126-b308-5a66-982f-9551d49ce414",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: French Bulldog, American Bulldog\n- People: Brigitte\n- Roles: dog actress\n- Concepts: dog breeds, breed types, breed origins\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1800s, Frenchies resulted from a cross between bulldog ancestors imported from England and local ratters in Paris, France.\n- Brigitte was born in 2010.\n- The French Bulldog, also known as the Frenchie, is a small breed of domestic dog.\n- The American Bulldog is a breed of utility dog.\n- The American Bulldog has two specific types, Standard and Classic, and also includes mixes of the two types.\n- Brigitte is a French Bulldog dog actress best known for her role as Stella in the ABC television series \"Modern Family\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d558a279-02e7-58e1-a290-92f1a482cbe7",
        "text": "Page: French Bulldog. Sentence: The French Bulldog also known as the Frenchie is a small breed of domestic dog.\nPage: French Bulldog. Sentence: Frenchies were the result in the 1800s of a cross between bulldog ancestors imported from England and local ratters in Paris (France).\nPage: American Bulldog. Sentence: The American Bulldog is a breed of utility dog.\nPage: American Bulldog. Sentence: There are two specific types of American Bulldog, Standard and Classic; additionally, there are also mixes of the two types.\nPage: Brigitte (dog). Sentence: Brigitte (born 2010) is a French Bulldog dog actress best known for her role as Stella in the ABC television series \"Modern Family\".",
